# Formats and lints staged files only, so the hook stays fast enough not to be
# disabled. Runs on the host rather than in the compose stack: a hook that fails
# when the stack is down is a hook people bypass, and host and container are both
# linux/glibc/amd64 so the same node_modules works in either — see docker-compose.yml.
#
# Invoked through node_modules/.bin rather than through pnpm, because a git hook
# gets a bare PATH and pnpm arrives via corepack shims that are not on it.
./node_modules/.bin/lint-staged

# Cheap, and the one boundary check no tool provides. Kept out of lint-staged
# because it is about the repository rather than about the files being committed.
node tools/check-contours.mjs
